From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matus <dichhead@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:27:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] target/arm/kvm: run VMApple guests under KVM

Forward Apple's pointer authentication hypercalls to QEMU with an SMCCC
filter and serve them by writing the vCPU's key registers, as
aquarat/qemu-reims-vgpu does on Asahi Linux.  Hosts without Apple's EL0
key registers share EL1's keys with EL0.  Wire every CPU PPI and the KVM
PMU on vmapple, and let it build with KVM alone.
---
